[2026-08-24T08:26:40+08:00] PROMPT 2 — technique analysis (written to prompt-2-techniques.txt, executed)
  Static source reading of all 8 repos. ~/similar-projects/TECHNIQUES.md.

  THE FINDING OF THIS PASS: p-e-w/heretic - 28,052 stars, 5,000+ derived models on
  HuggingFace, the field's reference tool - scores refusal with a 41-marker SUBSTRING
  MATCHER (src/heretic/scorers/keyword_rate.py). The marker list includes not just
  "i cannot" and "as an ai" but the content words "illegal", "harmful", "violat",
  "prohibit", "inappropriate", "unethical". Two consequences, and this metric IS the
  optimisation objective of its Optuna search:
    - a substantive compliant answer that uses the word "illegal" scores as a REFUSAL;
    - a fluent non-answer that avoids the marker words scores as a SUCCESS.
  The second is the empty-jailbreak failure mode StrongREJECT exists to catch, and the
  one ~/qwen2's own paper section 3.1a documented in its jailbreak arm. To the author's
  credit, empty responses are explicitly classified as matches "to avoid optimizing for
  them" - the reward-hacking risk was seen and the most obvious case patched, but not
  the general one.
  Corollary: heretic's "3/100 refusals" is NOT commensurable with ~/qwen2's "refusal
  rate 0.543". If heretic is used to produce models, its own score must be discarded
  and the models re-measured on the existing harness.

  Second finding: Arditi's refusal_direction is the only pipeline with a POSITIVE
  CONTROL - select_direction.py filters candidates on bypass score AND
  induce_refusal_threshold (adding the direction must INCREASE refusal) AND a hard
  kl_threshold=0.1. heretic drops the induce test and optimises for removal only.

  Third finding, and the practical one: THE RECIPE-VARIANCE ARM IS FEASIBLE ON THE 3090.
  heretic's model.py:402-405 special-cases Qwen3.5 hybrid layers, reading
  layer.linear_attn.out_proj for the GatedDeltaNet layers alongside self_attn.o_proj -
  the exact 64-layer / full_attention_interval=4 structure of the models under study.
  Not a README claim; it is in the source. It loads via BitsAndBytesConfig with
  configurable max_memory and dequantizes 4-bit per module, so 27B in 4-bit (~15 GB)
  fits with headroom. It needs HF safetensors, not GGUF (~54 GB download per base).
  Cheapest arm: one base (Qwen3.8-27B), two or three recipes, existing harness
  unchanged. Cheaper than the WMDP run hand-over.txt currently ranks above it.

  Also notable: ~/qwen2 is the ONLY project in the kept set using a rubric-based LLM
  judge that scores SUBSTANCE. Everything else uses keyword matching or logit-level
  refusal-token scores. On that axis the study is ahead of the tools it measures.

